    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n48213" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θεολογ-έω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>discourse on the gods and cosmology</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Metaph.</u>
				983b29
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">περί τινων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Mu.</u>
					391b4
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.614d
			</span></i>, etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Δία αὐτὸν [τὸν Φαέθοντα]
				ζωογόνον θεολογοῦσι</span>
			<i>call</i> him <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ζεύς ζ</span>. <i><span class="en">
				Antig.
				<u>Mir.</u>
				10b
			</span></i>:—
				Pass.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὰ θεολογούμενα</span>
			<i>discourses about the gods</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.421e
			</span></i> (v.l.), <i><span class="en">
				S.E.
				<u>M.</u>
				9.55
			</span></i>; title of work by Asclepiades of Mendes, <i><span class="en">
				Suet.
				<u>Aug.</u>
				94
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρεῖς αἱ Μοῖραι θεολογοῦνται</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>Theol.Ar.</u>
					16
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>refer to a divine influence</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοὺς
				τόκους</span> Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Ptol.
				<u>Tetr.</u>
				103
			</span></i>.</div>
